Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:18:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the legend of the table of the metadata levels says
 what its rows are for every picture

The legend under the table of the levels on the Dolby Vision page said "Used: Hades
reads its values and acts on them; the others it carries to the TV as they are". Of a
picture rebuilt as HDR10 or SDR the TV is sent none of the levels (its row "Sent to the
TV" is empty), and of native output some of those it is sent are made again (L5) or
held within their range (L1): the row says what the TV receives, the legend did not.

The legend names the two rows: "Used: Hades reads its values and acts on them. Sent:
what the TV receives." In es_es, es_ar and es_mx as well; shorter than before, so it
fits its box as the old one did.

Host test (outside the tree): t_legend.py fails on a legend that says the other levels
go to the TV (4 files before, none after); msgidsync.py: the Spanish files translate
the English of en_gb.
